  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Surface and Subsurface Mooring Data from Gulf of Alaska: Station GLOBEC 3",
  "description": "Surface and subsurface mooring data from Gulf of Alaska: Station GLOBEC 3. Data were collected from 1994 through 2004. Sampled months varied through the years but were usually during May, September, and October. Air temperature, barometric pressure, fluorometer, relative humidity, salinity, shortwave radiation, temperature, UV vector, velocity, and wind speed data were collected at various depths throughout the years using instruments such as ADCP, MicroCAT, MTR, RCM-9, SEACAT, and WeatherPAK. 188m was the maximum bottom depth.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect physical oceanographic properties at and near the mooring locations.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23568241",
